//? Title: TCN:causal tensors,weight normalization and visible clipped Adam
//? Subtitle: Tensor computations, explicit checks and reproducible local figures
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
A complete six-level temporal convolutional network classifies original GunPoint sequences. Exact prefix Jacobians,weight-normalization probes,explicit SGD references and every clipped Adam update show the computation alongside honest held-out failures.
)
\toc

Source example: `examples/cpp/source/nn/1_convolutional_neural_networks/1.9_1d_convolutions/tcn.cpp`.

> The method

Use two left-padded weight-normalized convolutions per residual level,dilations1..32,ReLU and explicit-generator dropout. A shared per-time binary head selects the last observed time. Save fitting-only normalization,train with explicit tensor global-norm clipping,and test causal prefixes plus all held-out source records without recomputing statistics.

The editable concept diagram is `diagrams/tcn_concept.tikz`. Regeneration uses
LaTeX with PGF/TikZ and standalone, plus dvisvgm; exports use the saved SVG.

```{bash, results="output", file="figures/tcn_concept.svg"}
set -eu
mkdir -p build
latex -interaction=batchmode -halt-on-error -output-directory=build diagrams/tcn_concept.tikz > build/tcn_concept.compile.log 2>&1
dvisvgm --no-fonts --bbox=10 --output=build/tcn_concept.svg build/tcn_concept.dvi > build/tcn_concept.render.log 2>&1
printf 'Rendered local concept diagram.\n'
```
