> Both widths retain all six residual levels

Full width64 has137,154 learned scalars;compact width8 has2,362. Both retain
40 learned leaves,6residual levels,dilations1/2/4/8/16/32,two convolutions per
level and the complete253-sample receptive field. Separate state contains
only fitting mean/std;there is no BN. Dropout keep.8 applies after each
convolution's ReLU during training,using an explicit generator. Inference
ignores dropout and supports any positive observed prefix length.
```{cpp, results="markdown", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>

#include <print>
int main() {
  namespace n = dm::nn;
  namespace m = n::models;
  n::set_num_threads(2);
  n::NoGradGuard guard;
  std::print("| width | learned values | leaves | scalar state | RF | every block shape | "
             "sequence | endpoint |\n|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---|---|---|\n");
  for (int width : {64, 8}) {
    n::ParameterStore p(461), state(463);
    m::TcnConfig c{width, 6, 3, 0, 1};
    const auto out = m::Tcn(p, state, n::ones({2, 150, 1}), c);
    std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | six times {} | {} | {} |\n", width, p.count(),
               p.size(), state.size(), m::TcnReceptiveField(c), out.blocks[0].shape(),
               out.sequence.shape(), out.logits.shape());
  }
}
