\image(figures/tcn_confusion.svg)
\caption(Complete true/predicted confusion counts for learned TCN and SGD centroid,sharing0..80 color range. True gun-draw0 is the bottom row;pointing1 is the top row.)
\alttext(Every held-out two-class count,including the learned TCN’s gun-draw failures.)

\image(figures/tcn_future.svg)
\caption(First actual held-out raw signal and a declared future-only perturbation from sample75. Earlier causal predictions coincide exactly;later predictions can differ. This is an input intervention,not an independent new source or accuracy test.)
\alttext(Actual original/perturbed signal and observed-prefix pointing probabilities,with no prefix normalization update.)

Selected epoch3 reduces fixed fitting CE4.985522 to.670643,but held-out
accuracy.426667 is below the untrained model.466667,the class0 tie.506667,
SGD centroid.660000 and raw1NN.906667. Its NLL.714699 improves over
untrained4.193172,while accuracy declines. The confusion11/65/21/53 exposes
frequent gun-draw failures. This run verifies implementation,not useful
classification or a TCN advantage. All15 gradient norms actually require clipping.

> Independent verification and limits

Six native tests execute full topology and every learned gradient,independent
weight-normalized causal equations and all20 tiny-coordinate finite differences,
exact field15 Jacobian/all reachable lags/future-zero/prefix equivalence,
actual held-out prefix gradients and future isolation,literal Float32 clipping
parity and invalid dropout/overflow checks. Public examples compile/run;
standalone header inclusion and the original three-epoch workflow pass.
Shared original-data and categorical metric/centroid oracles remain verified.

The source GunPoint records have collection and preprocessing dependencies.
A causal observed-input graph does not make them actor-disjoint or physically
online raw sensors. Tiny fitting/validation pools and short dropout training
limit accuracy conclusions;all actual held-out errors and baselines remain visible.

> Annotated confusion counts

The following program replots the complete frozen evaluation counts printed in the
predictor tables above. It reproduces those recorded measurements without refitting
or re-evaluating the model. `ConfusionMatrix::from_counts` owns the integer tensor
counts and `save_svg` labels every cell. True class zero is the **top** row and
predicted class zero the left column. Counts are exact; colors use the observed
count range. Source class meanings remain those declared for the dataset above.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/tcn_confusion_api_0.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <filesystem>
#include <print>
int main() {
  namespace n = dm::nn;
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  {
    const auto counts = n::from_vector(std::vector<std::int64_t>{11, 65, 21, 53}, {2, 2});
    const auto matrix = n::ConfusionMatrix::from_counts(counts);
    if (std::abs(matrix.accuracy() - 0.426667) > 1e-5)
      return 1;
    matrix.save_svg(
        "build/tcn_confusion_api_0.svg",
        {.title = "tcn / learned / 1", .cell_size = 52, .font_size = 13});
    std::print("Recorded evaluation 1: 150 observations; accuracy {:.6f}.\n", matrix.accuracy());
  }
}
```
